/.direnv/
# nix build symlink
/result
# The updaters now import a local module (update/fetch.py), so running them
# leaves bytecode behind. It has to stay ignored: the workflow decides
# whether to commit with `[ -n "$(git status -s)" ]`, and an untracked
# __pycache__ would make that true on every run, sending it into a
# `git commit` with nothing staged — which exits 1 and fails the job.
__pycache__/
